#
# Phase 1 step 7, the last step of the backbone: minimal repository understanding.
#
# What this image adds: `services/reference-control-plane/src/repo-map.mjs` — language
# detection, entry points, a symbol index, literal search, a dependency map, all read-only —
# and three routes (`GET /api/v1/repo-map`, `POST /api/v1/repo-map/scan`,
# `GET /api/v1/repo-map/search`), workspace-scoped and gated behind `workspace.read`.
#
# No Rust twin, on purpose: this reads a tree and reports what is in it, it does not decide
# or confine anything on the answer. Steps 1/3/4/5/6 got a Rust counterpart because they do —
# the stack split in 11_REVISIONE_E_CORREZIONI.md D-A. There is nothing here for a shared
# conformance oracle to hold two implementations equal to, so there is no oracle.
#
# The method is a heuristic and says so: `repoMapStatus()` declares `astParsing:false`,
# `incremental:false`, `secondLevelSignals:false` — ownership, recency, per-module coverage,
# criticality and fragility stay in phase 2 (09_PIANO.md P5). Symbol extraction is
# per-language regex over source text, not a parser.
#
# Only `services/reference-control-plane/src/` changed. Nothing else in the image is
# rebuilt or re-copied — an unchanged layer proves nothing and costs one anyway.
#
# Built with --network=none --pull=false.
FROM noesar-evolution:phase4-cow

USER root
COPY --chown=10001:10001 services/reference-control-plane/src/ /opt/noesar/services/reference-control-plane/src/
USER 10001:10001
